# Which browsers the build supports. The first four lines are Next.js's own
# defaults. The last line is for smart-TV browsers (Samsung Tizen, LG webOS,
# Android TV), which run old Chrome engines. Without it the CSS minifier
# removes the plain fallback values written in front of clamp(), max() and
# similar, and those TVs show pages without their pictures. It only keeps
# fallbacks; current browsers look and behave the same.
chrome >= 111
edge >= 111
firefox >= 111
safari >= 16.4
chrome >= 63
